Decades of conflict have contributed to&#13;
 high flows of internal displacement in Iraq. The incidence&#13;
 of these flows on the welfare of internally displaced&#13;
 persons is not well understood. This paper attempts to fill&#13;
 this gap in the literature by investigating the link between&#13;
 internal displacement and multidimensional poverty, using&#13;
 one of the most comprehensive household surveys for poverty&#13;
 analysis in Iraq. The results show crucial differences&#13;
 between internally displaced and non-displaced households&#13;
 with respect to multidimensional poverty. Furthermore,&#13;
 instrumental variable regression analysis suggests that the&#13;
 relationship is causal, that is, the probabilities of&#13;
 multidimensional and monetary poverty are higher because of&#13;
 internal displacement.
